# Files that run on the Jetson (bash, systemd, Python 3.10, the Uno sketch)
# must reach it with LF line endings: bash reads "\r" as part of a command
# ("$'\r': command not found"), systemd rejects or mis-parses CRLF unit lines,
# and a CRLF shebang ("python3\r") does not exec. This checkout is used from
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise write CRLF into the
# working tree, and a file copied from there to the Jetson (scp, USB stick)
# carries it along. Pinned by tests/test_mvp_flow.py (TestLineEndings).
#
# Deliberately NOT a repo-wide rule: the rest of the repository mixes
# endings, and forcing eol on everything would rewrite unrelated files.
#
# Everything under jetson/ is deployed to the board; text=auto leaves any
# binary that is ever added there untouched. The rules below it come later,
# so they win for the file types that are always text.
jetson/**     text=auto eol=lf
*.sh          text eol=lf
scripts/*.sh  text eol=lf
*.service     text eol=lf
*.target      text eol=lf
*.ino         text eol=lf
# This file too: the test that pins these rules reads it byte for byte.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
